chars | No effect |\\n   110→| 8 | Hard-coded death relationship detection | No effect |\\n   111→\\n   112→### The Fundamental Problem\\n   113→\\n   114→After 8 attempts, we have tried:\\n   115→- LLM prompt modifications (attempts 3, 5)\\n   116→- Structural pre-filters (attempts 4, 8)\\n   117→- Context window increases (attempt 7)\\n   118→- Death relationship detection (attempt 8)\\n   119→\\n   120→**None have worked.** The merge is happening despite ALL of these fixes.\\n   121→\\n   122→### Hypotheses for Why Fixes Keep Failing\\n   123→\\n   124→1. **The merge may happen BEFORE cross-group resolution**: The epithet \\\"the mummer\\\" may be classified and merged at an earlier pipeline stage before any of our checks run\\n   125→\\n   126→2. **The LLM merge decision is overriding all rules**: Even with explicit blocking code, the final merge decision may be bypassing these checks\\n   127→\\n   128→3. **Logging gap**: We haven't verified that the blocking code is actually being called. Need to add explicit debug logging to trace the exact point where the merge decision is made\\n   129→\\n   130→4. **The fix code may not be in the execution path**: The `_entities_in_death_relationship()` and `_entities_in_confrontation()` functions may exist but never be invoked\\n   131→\\n   132→### Recommended Next Approach\\n   133→\\n   134→**STOP adding new detection code until we verify existing code is being called.**\\n   135→\\n   136→1. **Add trace logging at EVERY decision point** in the character extraction pipeline:\\n   137→   - Log when epithet candidates are generated\\n   138→   - Log when cross-group resolution is called\\n   139→   - Log when confrontation/death checks are executed\\n   140→   - Log the exact LLM prompt and response for the merge decision\\n   141→   - Log the final merge output\\n   142→\\n   143→2. **Identify the EXACT line of code** where \\\"the mummer\\\" gets added to Prince Prospero's alias list\\n   144→\\n   145→3. **Consider fundamentally different approach**:\\n   146→   - Instead of trying to prevent the merge, post-process to SPLIT incorrectly merged characters\\n   147→   - Use the chapter summary (which correctly identifies 2 characters) to validate character extraction\\n   148→\\n   149→## Fix History\\n   150→\\n   151→### Attempt 8 Fixes Applied\\n   152→1. **Death relationship detection** (consensus.py)\\n   153→   - Root cause: `src/pipeline/character_extraction/consensus.py:_llm_cross_group_resolution()`\\n   154→   - Added `_entities_in_death_relationship()` function\\n   155→   - Detects patterns like \\\"fell prostrate in death\\\" + entity name co-occurrence\\n   156→   - **Result: DID NOT WORK** - merge still happening\\n   157→\\n   158→### Attempt 1-7 Fixes\\n   159→See previous evaluation state for full history.\\n   160→\\n   161→## Output Files\\n   162→- HTML: output/masque_of_red_death/report.html\\n   163→- JSON: output/masque_of_red_death/analysis.json\\n   164→\\n   165→## Key Observation\\n   166→\\n   167→**The chapter summary pipeline CORRECTLY identifies 2 characters:**\\n   168→- \\\"Prince Prospero\\\"\\n   169→- \\\"The masked figure (Red Death)\\\"\\n   170→\\n   171→**But the character extraction pipeline merges them into 1.**\\n   172→\\n   173→This proves the information is available - the character extraction pipeline is making a wrong decision.\\n   174→\\n   175→## Next Action\\n   176→\\n   177→Run PROMPT_fix.md with focus on:\\n   178→1. Add comprehensive debug logging to trace exactly WHERE the merge decision is made\\n   179→2. Verify that blocking code is actually being executed\\n   180→3. Consider post-processing approach to split incorrectly merged characters\\n   181→\\n\\n<system-reminder>\\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\\n</system-reminder>\\n\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"70ad5c5b-4289-44e9-b3de-238a550757a1\",\"uuid\":\"e87a9ee2-9628-4ad0-810a-951526e516c0\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/zacharymandrews/Tools/audiobook_agent/EVALUATION_STATE.md\",\"content\":\"# Current Evaluation State\\n\\n## Active Text\\n- **Name:** masque_of_red_death\\n- **Attempt:** 8\\n- **Phase:** awaiting_fix\\n- **baseline_score:** 6.75\\n\\n## Latest Scores\\n- Structure Detection: 10/10\\n- Character Extraction: 3/10 ← CRITICAL FAILURE (8 consecutive attempts failed)\\n- Character Profiles: 6/10\\n- Chapter Summaries: 9/10\\n- Pronunciation Guide: 6/10\\n- HTML Presentation: 8/10\\n- **Overall: 6.85/10** (threshold: 8.0)\\n\\n## Score Delta from Baseline (Attempt 1)\\n- Structure: 10 → 10 (unchanged)\\n- Characters: 5 → 3 (**-2 REGRESSION** from attempt 1)\\n- Profiles: 2 → 6 (+4 improvement)\\n- Summaries: 9 → 9 (unchanged)\\n- Pronunciation: 5 → 6 (+1 improvement)\\n- Presentation: 9 → 8 (-1 regression)\\n- **Overall: 6.75 → 6.85 (+0.10 slight improvement)**\\n\\n## Attempt 8 Fix Assessment\\n\\n### Fix: Hard-coded death relationship detection\\n**Status: DID NOT WORK**\\n\\nThe fix from attempt 8 added `_entities_in_death_relationship()` function to detect when one entity dies at the hands of another. This was meant to block the merge of \\\"the mummer\\\" with \\\"Prince Prospero\\\" based on the text:\\n- \\\"fell prostrate in death the Prince Prospero\\\" (Prospero dies)\\n- \\\"seizing the mummer\\\" (after Prospero confronts the mummer)\\n\\n**Result:** \\\"the mummer\\\" is STILL incorrectly merged with \\\"Prince Prospero\\\"\\n\\n**Evidence from analysis.json:**\\n- Character: \\\"the Prince Prospero\\\"\\n- Aliases: [\\\"the mummer\\\"]\\n- Only 1 character detected (should be 2)\\n\\n**Why it failed:** Possible reasons:\\n1. The death relationship function may not be getting called\\n2. The merge may be happening at an earlier pipeline stage\\n3. The function's pattern matching may not be capturing the actual text patterns\\n4. The merge decision may be bypassing the death relationship check\\n\\n## Current Issues (Priority Order)\\n\\n### CRITICAL\\n1. **False character merge: \\\"the mummer\\\" merged with Prince Prospero**\\n   - Problem: \\\"the mummer\\\" is listed as an alias of Prince Prospero, but it refers to the Red Death personification - THE MAIN ANTAGONIST\\n   - Evidence from text:\\n     - \\\"seizing the mummer, whose tall figure stood erect and motionless within the shadow of the ebony clock\\\"\\n     - \\\"fell prostrate in death the Prince Prospero\\\" (Prospero DIES after confronting the mummer)\\n     - The mummer is described as \\\"dressed as the Red Death itself, draped in grave-cloths\\\"\\n   - Impact: The main antagonist is merged with the protagonist (-2 point character score minimum)\\n   - **EIGHT attempts have now failed to fix this issue**\\n   - Location: `src/pipeline/character_extraction/consensus.py`\\n\\n2. **Missing character: The Red Death / Masked Figure**\\n   - Problem: The antagonist of the story should be its own character entry\\n   - Aliases that should be grouped together:\\n     - \\\"the figure\\\" / \\\"the masked figure\\\"\\n     - \\\"the stranger\\\"\\n     - \\\"the intruder\\\"\\n     - \\\"the mummer\\\"\\n     - \\\"the Red Death\\\" (personification)\\n   - Evidence: Chapter summary CORRECTLY identifies two characters: \\\"Prince Prospero\\\" and \\\"The masked figure (Red Death)\\\" - but character extraction merges them\\n   - Impact: Major character missing from analysis\\n   - Note: Will emerge naturally once issue #1 is fixed\\n\\n### HIGH\\n3. **Missing alias: \\\"the duke\\\" for Prince Prospero**\\n   - Problem: Text uses \\\"the duke\\\" to refer to Prospero: \\\"as might have been expected from the duke's love of the bizarre\\\"\\n   - Location: Alias detection\\n\\n4. **Mention count too low for Prince Prospero**\\n   - Problem: Character shows 6 mentions, but pronunciation shows 18 \\\"Prospero\\\" + 9 \\\"Prince\\\" occurrences\\n   - Evidence: Clear discrepancy between pronunciation counting and character counting\\n   - Location: Mention count aggregation in character pipeline\\n\\n### MEDIUM\\n5. **Canonical name format includes leading article**\\n   - Problem: Character name is \\\"the Prince Prospero\\\" instead of \\\"Prince Prospero\\\"\\n   - Location: Character name normalization\\n\\n6. **Too many common words in pronunciation guide (65+ in \\\"Other\\\")**\\n   - Problem: Common words like \\\"dauntless\\\", \\\"chiming\\\", \\\"magnificence\\\", \\\"casements\\\" are flagged\\n   - Location: Pronunciation flagging threshold\\n\\n7. **Foreign word false positive: \\\"decorum\\\"**\\n   - Problem: \\\"decorum\\\" flagged as foreign word - it's standard English (Latin-derived but fully assimilated)\\n   - Location: Foreign word detection\\n\\n## Root Cause Analysis: Why 8 Attempts Have Failed\\n\\n### Summary of All Failed Attempts\\n\\n| Attempt | Fix Applied | Result |\\n|---------|-------------|--------|\\n| 1 | Cross-group epithet resolution | No effect |\\n| 2 | Proper name with article classification | Caused regression - merge started |\\n| 3 | Added CRITICAL RULE #5 about confrontation in prompt | No effect |\\n| 4 | Implemented `_entities_in_confrontation()` function | No effect |\\n| 5 | Solo pattern matching for confrontation | No effect |\\n| 6 | (Evaluation only, no new fix) | No effect |\\n| 7 | Increased context window 150/120 → 400 chars | No effect |\\n| 8 | Hard-coded death relationship detection | No effect |\\n\\n### The Fundamental Problem\\n\\nAfter 8 attempts, we have tried:\\n- LLM prompt modifications (attempts 3, 5)\\n- Structural pre-filters (attempts 4, 8)\\n- Context window increases (attempt 7)\\n- Death relationship detection (attempt 8)\\n\\n**None have worked.** The merge is happening despite ALL of these fixes.\\n\\n### Hypotheses for Why Fixes Keep Failing\\n\\n1. **The merge may happen BEFORE cross-group resolution**: The epithet \\\"the mummer\\\" may be classified and merged at an earlier pipeline stage before any of our checks run\\n\\n2. **The LLM merge decision is overriding all rules**: Even with explicit blocking code, the final merge decision may be bypassing these checks\\n\\n3. **Logging gap**: We haven't verified that the blocking code is actually being called. Need to add explicit debug logging to trace the exact point where the merge decision is made\\n\\n4. **The fix code may not be in the execution path**: The `_entities_in_death_relationship()` and `_entities_in_confrontation()` functions may exist but never be invoked\\n\\n### Recommended Next Approach\\n\\n**STOP adding new detection code until we verify existing code is being called.**\\n\\n1. **Add trace logging at EVERY decision point** in the character extraction pipeline:\\n   - Log when epithet candidates are generated\\n   - Log when cross-group resolution is called\\n   - Log when confrontation/death checks are executed\\n   - Log the exact LLM prompt and response for the merge decision\\n   - Log the final merge output\\n\\n2. **Identify the EXACT line of code** where \\\"the mummer\\\" gets added to Prince Prospero's alias list\\n\\n3. **Consider fundamentally different approach**:\\n   - Instead of trying to prevent the merge, post-process to SPLIT incorrectly merged characters\\n   - Use the chapter summary (which correctly identifies 2 characters) to validate character extraction\\n\\n## Fix History\\n\\n### Attempt 8 Fixes Applied\\n1. **Death relationship detection** (consensus.py)\\n   - Root cause: `src/pipeline/character_extraction/consensus.py:_llm_cross_group_resolution()`\\n   - Added `_entities_in_death_relationship()` function\\n   - Detects patterns like \\\"fell prostrate in death\\\" + entity name co-occurrence\\n   - **Result: DID NOT WORK** - merge still happening\\n\\n### Attempt 1-7 Fixes\\nSee previous evaluation state for full history.\\n\\n## Output Files\\n- HTML: output/masque_of_red_death/report.html\\n- JSON: output/masque_of_red_death/analysis.json\\n\\n## Key Observation\\n\\n**The chapter summary pipeline CORRECTLY identifies 2 characters:**\\n- \\\"Prince Prospero\\\"\\n- \\\"The masked figure (Red Death)\\\"\\n\\n**But the character extraction pipeline merges them into 1.**\\n\\nThis proves the information is available - the character extraction pipeline is making a wrong decision.\\n\\n## Next Action\\n\\nRun PROMPT_fix.md with focus on:\\n1. Add comprehensive debug logging to trace exactly WHERE the merge decision is made\\n2. Verify that blocking code is actually being executed\\n3. Consider post-processing approach to split incorrectly merged characters\\n\",\"numLines\":181,\"startLine\":1,\"totalLines\":181}}}\n{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01CKgwvFYkbqN6mNTPfkW7xH\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"     1→# Audiobook Prep Output Quality Rubric\\n     2→\\n     3→This rubric defines evaluation criteria for audiobook narrator preparation documents. Use this to assess analysis output quality.\\n     4→\\n     5→## Scoring Overview\\n     6→\\n     7→| Category | Weight | Focus |\\n     8→|----------|--------|-------|\\n     9→| Structure Detection | 20% | Chapter boundaries, front/back matter |\\n    10→| Character Extraction | 25% | All characters identified, correct aliases |\\n    11→| Character Profiles | 15% | Accurate descriptions, relationships |\\n    12→| Chapter Summaries | 20% | Key events, narrator-useful details |\\n    13→| Pronunciation Guide | 10% | Unusual words flagged, no false positives |\\n    14→| HTML Presentation | 10% | Navigation, readability, organization |\\n    15→\\n    16→**Threshold:** Overall score >= 8.0 to pass\\n    17→\\n    18→---\\n    19→\\n    20→## Category Details\\n    21→\\n    22→### 1. Structure Detection (Weight: 20%)\\n    23→\\n    24→**What we're measuring:** Did the tool correctly identify the book's organization?\\n    25→\\n    26→| Score | Criteria |\\n    27→|-------|----------|\\n    28→| 10 | Perfect: All chapters identified, correct boundaries, handles unusual structures |\\n    29→| 8-9 | Excellent: All major divisions correct, minor issues with epigraphs or breaks |\\n    30→| 6-7 | Good: Most chapters correct, some boundary errors or missed subdivisions |\\n    31→| 4-5 | Fair: Significant errors but majority of structure captured |\\n    32→| 1-3 | Poor: Major structural errors, merged or missing chapters |\\n    33→| 0 | Failed: Structure completely wrong or not detected |\\n    34→\\n    35→**Checklist:**\\n    36→- [ ] All chapters detected (compare to expected chapter count)\\n    37→- [ ] Chapter titles extracted correctly\\n    38→- [ ] Front matter (dedication, preface) identified separately\\n    39→- [ ] Back matter (notes, appendices) identified separately\\n    40→- [ ] No merged chapters (two chapters treated as one)\\n    41→- [ ] No split chapters (one chapter treated as multiple)\\n    42→- [ ] Roman numerals handled correctly\\n    43→- [ ] \\\"Chapter\\\" vs \\\"Book\\\" vs \\\"Part\\\" hierarchy correct\\n    44→\\n    45→---\\n    46→\\n    47→### 2. Character Extraction (Weight: 25%)\\n    48→\\n    49→**What we're measuring:** Are all significant characters identified with correct information?\\n    50→\\n    51→| Score | Criteria |\\n    52→|-------|----------|\\n    53→| 10 | Perfect: All named characters, correct aliases, accurate relationships |\\n    54→| 8-9 | Excellent: All major characters, most minor, few alias issues |\\n    55→| 6-7 | Good: Major characters correct, some missing minors or alias errors |\\n    56→| 4-5 | Fair: Main characters present but significant gaps or errors |\\n    57→| 1-3 | Poor: Major characters missing or incorrectly merged/split |\\n    58→| 0 | Failed: Character extraction completely wrong |\\n    59→\\n    60→**Checklist:**\\n    61→- [ ] All major characters (>10 mentions) identified\\n    62→- [ ] No false character splits (same person as two entries)\\n    63→- [ ] No false character merges (two people as one entry)\\n    64→- [ ] Aliases correctly grouped (full name = nickname = title+name)\\n    65→- [ ] Titles handled correctly (Dr., Mr., Mrs., etc.)\\n    66→- [ ] Nicknames linked to canonical names\\n    67→- [ ] No hallucinated characters (entries that don't exist in text)\\n    68→- [ ] First appearance chapter is accurate\\n    69→\\n    70→**Common Issues:**\\n    71→- Characters sharing surnames incorrectly merged (spouses, siblings)\\n    72→- Full names and nicknames not linked\\n    73→- Titled references (Mr. X) not linked to full names\\n    74→- Minor characters filtered out too aggressively\\n    75→\\n    76→---\\n    77→\\n    78→### 3. Character Profiles (Weight: 15%)\\n    79→\\n    80→**What we're measuring:** Are character descriptions accurate and useful for narration?\\n    81→\\n    82→| Score | Criteria |\\n    83→|-------|----------|\\n    84→| 10 | Perfect: Rich, accurate descriptions with voice notes and relationships |\\n    85→| 8-9 | Excellent: Good descriptions, accurate relationships, useful details |\\n    86→| 6-7 | Good: Basic descriptions correct, some missing depth |\\n    87→| 4-5 | Fair: Descriptions present but thin or partially inaccurate |\\n    88→| 1-3 | Poor: Descriptions wrong or mostly missing |\\n    89→| 0 | Failed: No useful profile information |\\n    90→\\n    91→**Checklist:**\\n    92→- [ ] Physical descriptions match text (when provided)\\n    93→- [ ] Personality traits supported by text evidence\\n    94→- [ ] Key relationships identified (family, romantic, professional)\\n    95→- [ ] No invented details (information not in the source text)\\n    96→- [ ] Speech patterns or dialect noted (when present)\\n    97→- [ ] Character arc summary useful for narrator\\n    98→\\n    99→---\\n   100→\\n   101→### 4. Chapter Summaries (Weight: 20%)\\n   102→\\n   103→**What we're measuring:** Do summaries help a narrator prepare for each chapter?\\n   104→\\n   105→| Score | Criteria |\\n   106→|-------|----------|\\n   107→| 10 | Perfect: Accurate, comprehensive, narrator-focused summaries |\\n   108→| 8-9 | Excellent: Captures key events and tone, useful for prep |\\n   109→| 6-7 | Good: Main events correct, some gaps or minor errors |\\n   110→| 4-5 | Fair: Partially accurate but missing key events or has errors |\\n   111→| 1-3 | Poor: Major inaccuracies or missing most content |\\n   112→| 0 | Failed: Summaries wrong or not generated |\\n   113→\\n   114→**Checklist:**\\n   115→- [ ] Key plot events captured (3-5 per chapter minimum)\\n   116→- [ ] Characters appearing in chapter mentioned\\n   117→- [ ] No hallucinated events (things that didn't happen)\\n   118→- [ ] No major spoilers from future chapters\\n   119→- [ ] Tone and mood indicated (useful for narrator)\\n   120→- [ ] Length appropriate (100-300 words)\\n   121→- [ ] Setting/location changes noted\\n   122→\\n   123→---\\n   124→\\n   125→### 5. Pronunciation Guide (Weight: 10%)\\n   126→\\n   127→**What we're measuring:** Are unusual words flagged with helpful pronunciation info?\\n   128→\\n   129→| Score | Criteria |\\n   130→|-------|----------|\\n   131→| 10 | Perfect: All unusual words flagged, accurate IPA, no false positives |\\n   132→| 8-9 | Excellent: Good coverage, mostly accurate, few false positives |\\n   133→| 6-7 | Good: Most unusual words caught, some gaps or errors |\\n   134→| 4-5 | Fair: Partial coverage, noticeable gaps or many false positives |\\n   135→| 1-3 | Poor: Major gaps or mostly incorrect |\\n   136→| 0 | Failed: No useful pronunciation information |\\n   137→\\n   138→**Checklist:**\\n   139→- [ ] Foreign words/phrases identified\\n   140→- [ ] Unusual proper nouns flagged (names, places)\\n   141→- [ ] Period-specific terms noted\\n   142→- [ ] IPA provided and accurate (when present)\\n   143→- [ ] No common words flagged (false positives)\\n   144→- [ ] Context provided for homographs (read vs. read, lead vs. lead)\\n   145→- [ ] Regional/dialect pronunciations noted\\n   146→\\n   147→---\\n   148→\\n   149→### 6. HTML Presentation (Weight: 10%)\\n   150→\\n   151→**What we're measuring:** Is the output professional and usable?\\n   152→\\n   153→| Score | Criteria |\\n   154→|-------|----------|\\n   155→| 10 | Perfect: Clean, navigable, print-ready, professional appearance |\\n   156→| 8-9 | Excellent: Well-organized, easy to use, minor polish issues |\\n   157→| 6-7 | Good: Functional and readable, some UX improvements possible |\\n   158→| 4-5 | Fair: Usable but awkward navigation or formatting issues |\\n   159→| 1-3 | Poor: Difficult to use, significant formatting problems |\\n   160→| 0 | Failed: Broken or unreadable |\\n   161→\\n   162→**Checklist:**\\n   163→- [ ] Navigation works (can jump to chapters, characters)\\n   164→- [ ] Typography is readable\\n   165→- [ ] Information is logically organized\\n   166→- [ ] No broken elements or missing sections\\n   167→- [ ] Prints cleanly (if applicable)\\n   168→\\n   169→---\\n   170→\\n   171→## Scoring Formula\\n   172→\\n   173→```\\n   174→Overall = (\\n   175→    Structure × 0.20 +\\n   176→    Characters × 0.25 +\\n   177→    Profiles × 0.15 +\\n   178→    Summaries × 0.20 +\\n   179→    Pronunciation × 0.10 +\\n   180→    Presentation × 0.10\\n   181→)\\n   182→```\\n   183→\\n   184→**Thresholds:**\\n   185→- **>= 8.0**: PASS - advance to next text\\n   186→- **< 8.0**: FAIL - iterate with fixes\\n   187→\\n   188→---\\n   189→\\n   190→## Issue Severity Classification\\n   191→\\n   192→When scoring below threshold, classify issues for the fix phase:\\n   193→\\n   194→### CRITICAL (blocks progress, score impact > 1 point)\\n   195→- Character merge/split errors for main characters\\n   196→- Missing major characters\\n   197→- Completely wrong chapter structure\\n   198→- Hallucinated content\\n   199→\\n   200→### HIGH (significant impact, score impact 0.5-1 point)\\n   201→- Missing minor but named characters\\n   202→- Incorrect relationships for main characters\\n   203→- Multiple chapter summary errors\\n   204→- Major pronunciation gaps\\n   205→\\n   206→### MEDIUM (noticeable but manageable, score impact < 0.5)\\n   207→- Minor character description inaccuracies\\n   208→- Excessive false positives in pronunciation\\n   209→- Formatting/presentation issues\\n   210→- Missing some aliases\\n   211→\\n   212→### LOW (polish items)\\n   213→- Minor wording improvements\\n   214→- Edge case handling\\n   215→- Performance optimizations\\n   216→\\n   217→---\\n   218→\\n   219→## Evaluation Notes\\n   220→\\n   221→### Use Your Knowledge\\n   222→The evaluator (Claude) has literary knowledge of classic texts. Use this knowledge to:\\n   223→- Verify character completeness against known casts\\n   224→- Check summary accuracy against known plots\\n   225→- Validate relationships and aliases\\n   226→\\n   227→### Be Specific\\n   228→Instead of: \\\"Character extraction has issues\\\"\\n   229→Write: \\\"Jay Gatsby and 'Gatsby' are listed as separate characters. These should be merged as aliases.\\\"\\n   230→\\n   231→### Be Actionable\\n   232→Include file locations and suggested fixes when possible:\\n   233→- \\\"Likely cause: alias resolution in src/agents/characters.py\\\"\\n   234→- \\\"Suggested fix: improve fuzzy matching for FirstName-LastName to LastName\\\"\\n   235→\\n   236→### Focus on Threshold\\n   237→If score is 7.8, focus only on what's needed to cross 8.0. Don't enumerate every possible improvement.\\n   238→\\n\\n<system-reminder>\\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\\n</system-reminder>\\n\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"70ad5c5b-4289-44e9-b3de-238a550757a1\",\"uuid\":\"37440195-8146-4791-a022-a36799d3f7b5\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/zacharymandrews/Tools/audiobook_agent/spec/output_quality.md\",\"content\":\"# Audiobook Prep Output Quality Rubric\\n\\nThis rubric defines evaluation criteria for audiobook narrator preparation documents. Use this to assess analysis output quality.\\n\\n## Scoring Overview\\n\\n| Category | Weight | Focus |\\n|----------|--------|-------|\\n| Structure Detection | 20% | Chapter boundaries, front/back matter |\\n| Character Extraction | 25% | All characters identified, correct aliases |\\n| Character Profiles | 15% | Accurate descriptions, relationships |\\n| Chapter Summaries | 20% | Key events, narrator-useful details |\\n| Pronunciation Guide | 10% | Unusual words flagged, no false positives |\\n| HTML Presentation | 10% | Navigation, readability, organization |\\n\\n**Threshold:** Overall score >= 8.0 to pass\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Category Details\\n\\n### 1. Structure Detection (Weight: 20%)\\n\\n**What we're measuring:** Did the tool correctly identify the book's organization?\\n\\n| Score | Criteria |\\n|-------|----------|\\n| 10 | Perfect: All chapters identified, correct boundaries, handles unusual structures |\\n| 8-9 | Excellent: All major divisions correct, minor issues with epigraphs or breaks |\\n| 6-7 | Good: Most chapters correct, some boundary errors or missed subdivisions |\\n| 4-5 | Fair: Significant errors but majority of structure captured |\\n| 1-3 | Poor: Major structural errors, merged or missing chapters |\\n| 0 | Failed: Structure completely wrong or not detected |\\n\\n**Checklist:**\\n- [ ] All chapters detected (compare to expected chapter count)\\n- [ ] Chapter titles extracted correctly\\n- [ ] Front matter (dedication, preface) identified separately\\n- [ ] Back matter (notes, appendices) identified separately\\n- [ ] No merged chapters (two chapters treated as one)\\n- [ ] No split chapters (one chapter treated as multiple)\\n- [ ] Roman numerals handled correctly\\n- [ ] \\\"Chapter\\\" vs \\\"Book\\\" vs \\\"Part\\\" hierarchy correct\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 2. Character Extraction (Weight: 25%)\\n\\n**What we're measuring:** Are all significant characters identified with correct information?\\n\\n| Score | Criteria |\\n|-------|----------|\\n| 10 | Perfect: All named characters, correct aliases, accurate relationships |\\n| 8-9 | Excellent: All major characters, most minor, few alias issues |\\n| 6-7 | Good: Major characters correct, some missing minors or alias errors |\\n| 4-5 | Fair: Main characters present but significant gaps or errors |\\n| 1-3 | Poor: Major characters missing or incorrectly merged/split |\\n| 0 | Failed: Character extraction completely wrong |\\n\\n**Checklist:**\\n- [ ] All major characters (>10 mentions) identified\\n- [ ] No false character splits (same person as two entries)\\n- [ ] No false character merges (two people as one entry)\\n- [ ] Aliases correctly grouped (full name = nickname = title+name)\\n- [ ] Titles handled correctly (Dr., Mr., Mrs., etc.)\\n- [ ] Nicknames linked to canonical names\\n- [ ] No hallucinated characters (entries that don't exist in text)\\n- [ ] First appearance chapter is accurate\\n\\n**Common Issues:**\\n- Characters sharing surnames incorrectly merged (spouses, siblings)\\n- Full names and nicknames not linked\\n- Titled references (Mr. X) not linked to full names\\n- Minor characters filtered out too aggressively\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 3. Character Profiles (Weight: 15%)\\n\\n**What we're measuring:** Are character descriptions accurate and useful for narration?\\n\\n| Score | Criteria |\\n|-------|----------|\\n| 10 | Perfect: Rich, accurate descriptions with voice notes and relationships |\\n| 8-9 | Excellent: Good descriptions, accurate relationships, useful details |\\n| 6-7 | Good: Basic descriptions correct, some missing depth |\\n| 4-5 | Fair: Descriptions present but thin or partially inaccurate |\\n| 1-3 | Poor: Descriptions wrong or mostly missing |\\n| 0 | Failed: No useful profile information |\\n\\n**Checklist:**\\n- [ ] Physical descriptions match text (when provided)\\n- [ ] Personality traits supported by text evidence\\n- [ ] Key relationships identified (family, romantic, professional)\\n- [ ] No invented details (information not in the source text)\\n- [ ] Speech patterns or dialect noted (when present)\\n- [ ] Character arc summary useful for narrator\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 4. Chapter Summaries (Weight: 20%)\\n\\n**What we're measuring:** Do summaries help a narrator prepare for each chapter?\\n\\n| Score | Criteria |\\n|-------|----------|\\n| 10 | Perfect: Accurate, comprehensive, narrator-focused summaries |\\n| 8-9 | Excellent: Captures key events and tone, useful for prep |\\n| 6-7 | Good: Main events correct, some gaps or minor errors |\\n| 4-5 | Fair: Partially accurate but missing key events or has errors |\\n| 1-3 | Poor: Major inaccuracies or missing most content |\\n| 0 | Failed: Summaries wrong or not generated |\\n\\n**Checklist:**\\n- [ ] Key plot events captured (3-5 per chapter minimum)\\n- [ ] Characters appearing in chapter mentioned\\n- [ ] No hallucinated events (things that didn't happen)\\n- [ ] No major spoilers from future chapters\\n- [ ] Tone and mood indicated (useful for narrator)\\n- [ ] Length appropriate (100-300 words)\\n- [ ] Setting/location changes noted\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 5. Pronunciation Guide (Weight: 10%)\\n\\n**What we're measuring:** Are unusual words flagged with helpful pronunciation info?\\n\\n| Score | Criteria |\\n|-------|----------|\\n| 10 | Perfect: All unusual words flagged, accurate IPA, no false positives |\\n| 8-9 | Excellent: Good coverage, mostly accurate, few false positives |\\n| 6-7 | Good: Most unusual words caught, some gaps or errors |\\n| 4-5 | Fair: Partial coverage, noticeable gaps or many false positives |\\n| 1-3 | Poor: Major gaps or mostly incorrect |\\n| 0 | Failed: No useful pronunciation information |\\n\\n**Checklist:**\\n- [ ] Foreign words/phrases identified\\n- [ ] Unusual proper nouns flagged (names, places)\\n- [ ] Period-specific terms noted\\n- [ ] IPA provided and accurate (when present)\\n- [ ] No common words flagged (false positives)\\n- [ ] Context provided for homographs (read vs. read, lead vs. lead)\\n- [ ] Regional/dialect pronunciations noted\\n\\n---\\n\\n### 6. HTML Presentation (Weight: 10%)\\n\\n**What we're measuring:** Is the output professional and usable?\\n\\n| Score | Criteria |\\n|-------|----------|\\n| 10 | Perfect: Clean, navigable, print-ready, professional appearance |\\n| 8-9 | Excellent: Well-organized, easy to use, minor polish issues |\\n| 6-7 | Good: Functional and readable, some UX improvements possible |\\n| 4-5 | Fair: Usable but awkward navigation or formatting issues |\\n| 1-3 | Poor: Difficult to use, significant formatting problems |\\n| 0 | Failed: Broken or unreadable |\\n\\n**Checklist:**\\n- [ ] Navigation works (can jump to chapters, characters)\\n- [ ] Typography is readable\\n- [ ] Information is logically organized\\n- [ ] No broken elements or missing sections\\n- [ ] Prints cleanly (if applicable)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Scoring Formula\\n\\n```\\nOverall = (\\n    Structure × 0.20 +\\n    Characters × 0.25 +\\n    Profiles × 0.15 +\\n    Summaries × 0.20 +\\n    Pronunciation × 0.10 +\\n    Presentation × 0.10\\n)\\n```\\n\\n**Thresholds:**\\n- **>= 8.0**: PASS - advance to next text\\n- **< 8.0**: FAIL - iterate with fixes\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Issue Severity Classification\\n\\nWhen scoring below threshold, classify issues for the fix phase:\\n\\n### CRITICAL (blocks progress, score impact > 1 point)\\n- Character merge/split errors for main characters\\n- Missing major characters\\n- Completely wrong chapter structure\\n- Hallucinated content\\n\\n### HIGH (significant impact, score impact 0.5-1 point)\\n- Missing minor but named characters\\n- Incorrect relationships for main characters\\n- Multiple chapter summary errors\\n- Major pronunciation gaps\\n\\n### MEDIUM (noticeable but manageable, score impact < 0.5)\\n- Minor character description inaccuracies\\n- Excessive false positives in pronunciation\\n- Formatting/presentation issues\\n- Missing some aliases\\n\\n### LOW (polish items)\\n- Minor wording improvements\\n- Edge case handling\\n- Performance optimizations\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Evaluation Notes\\n\\n### Use Your Knowledge\\nThe evaluator (Claude) has literary knowledge of classic texts. Use this knowledge to:\\n- Verify character completeness against known casts\\n- Check summary accuracy against known plots\\n- Validate relationships and aliases\\n\\n### Be Specific\\nInstead of: \\\"Character extraction has issues\\\"\\nWrite: \\\"Jay Gatsby and 'Gatsby' are listed as separate characters. These should be merged as aliases.\\\"\\n\\n### Be Actionable\\nInclude file locations and suggested fixes when possible:\\n- \\\"Likely cause: alias resolution in src/agents/characters.py\\\"\\n- \\\"Suggested fix: improve fuzzy matching for FirstName-LastName to LastName\\\"\\n\\n### Focus on Threshold\\nIf score is 7.8, focus only on what's needed to cross 8.0. Don't enumerate every possible improvement.\\n\",\"numLines\":238,\"startLine\":1,\"totalLines\":238}}}\n{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01GVP31PhLtxS4HiopgVEsvX\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"     1→# Audiobook Agent - Operational Guide\\n     2→\\n     3→This guide provides operational commands and codebase navigation for the autonomous improvement loop.\\n     4→\\n     5→## Running the Analysis Pipeline\\n     6→\\n     7→### Basic Commands\\n     8→\\n     9→```bash\\n    10→# Full analysis on a text file with HTML output (use --rich-progress for live updates)\\n    11→venv/bin/python -m src.cli analyze Test_Texts/gatsby.txt --html output/gatsby/report.html --output output/gatsby/analysis.json --rich-progress\\n    12→\\n    13→# With specific models per agent\\n    14→venv/bin/python -m src.cli analyze Test_Texts/gatsby.txt \\\\\\n    15→    --structure-model qwen2.5:14b \\\\\\n    16→    --character-model qwen2.5:32b \\\\\\n    17→    --summary-model qwen2.5:32b \\\\\\n    18→    --pronunciation-model qwen2.5:14b \\\\\\n    19→    --html output/gatsby/report.html \\\\\\n    20→    --rich-progress\\n    21→\\n    22→# Set default model for all agents\\n    23→venv/bin/python -m src.cli analyze Test_Texts/gatsby.txt --llm-model qwen2.5:32b --html output/gatsby/report.html --rich-progress\\n    24→\\n    25→# Adjust minimum character mentions threshold\\n    26→venv/bin/python -m src.cli analyze Test_Texts/gatsby.txt --min-mentions 3 --html output/gatsby/report.html --rich-progress\\n    27→```\\n    28→\\n    29→### CLI Options\\n    30→\\n    31→| Option | Description | Default |\\n    32→|--------|-------------|---------|\\n    33→| `--output FILE` | JSON output path | `{input_stem}.analysis.json` |\\n    34→| `--html FILE` | HTML report path | None |\\n    35→| `--tui` | Open interactive TUI after analysis | False |\\n    36→| `--wpm N` | Words per minute for duration estimates | 150 |\\n    37→| `--min-mentions N` | Minimum character mentions to include | 2 |\\n    38→| `--llm-model MODEL` | Default model for all agents | System default |\\n    39→| `--structure-model MODEL` | Model for chapter detection | Default |\\n    40→| `--character-model MODEL` | Model for character extraction | Default |\\n    41→| `--summary-model MODEL` | Model for chapter summaries | Default |\\n    42→| `--pronunciation-model MODEL` | Model for pronunciation flags | Default |\\n    43→| `--rich-progress` | Show live-updating progress display | False |\\n    44→\\n    45→## Output Locations\\n    46→\\n    47→```\\n    48→output/\\n    49→└── {book_name}/\\n    50→    ├── report.html          # HTML report for narrator prep\\n    51→    └── analysis.json        # Full JSON analysis data\\n    52→```\\n    53→\\n    54→## Test Texts\\n    55→\\n    56→Available in `Test_Texts/`:\\n    57→- `gatsby.txt` - The Great Gatsby (306 KB)\\n    58→- `Frankenstein_ebook.txt` - Frankenstein (421 KB)\\n    59→- `East of Eden - East Of Eden.pdf` - East of Eden (1.6 MB)\\n    60→- `I_Have_No_Mouth_And_I_Must_Scream.pdf` - Ellison short story (325 KB)\\n    61→- `One Hundred Years of Solitude - One_Hundred_Years_of_Solitude.pdf` - Marquez (1.5 MB)\\n    62→- `See the Light V-15 11-11-25.docx` - Test document (1.2 MB)\\n    63→\\n    64→## Key Source Files\\n    65→\\n    66→### Agent System\\n    67→| File | Purpose |\\n    68→|------|---------|\\n    69→| `src/agents/base.py` | Abstract Agent class with verify/refine methods |\\n    70→| `src/agents/structure.py` | StructureAgent - chapter detection |\\n    71→| `src/agents/characters.py` | CharacterAgent - character extraction & aliases |\\n    72→| `src/agents/summaries.py` | SummaryAgent - chapter summaries |\\n    73→| `src/agents/pronunciation.py` | PronunciationAgent - pronunciation flags |\\n    74→| `src/agents/config.py` | OrchestratorConfig, per-agent model settings |\\n    75→| `src/agents/validation.py` | Upstream validation types |\\n    76→\\n    77→### Pipeline\\n    78→| File | Purpose |\\n    79→|------|---------|\\n    80→| `src/analyzer.py` | Main orchestrator - runs all agents |\\n    81→| `src/pipeline/character_extraction/` | Character NER and extraction |\\n    82→| `src/pipeline/character_profiling/` | Character profile generation |\\n    83→| `src/pipeline/llm.py` | Unified LLM client (Ollama/OpenAI/Anthropic) |\\n    84→| `src/pipeline/metrics.py` | Profiling and metrics |\\n    85→\\n    86→### Entry Points\\n    87→| File | Purpose |\\n    88→|------|---------|\\n    89→| `src/cli.py` | CLI entry point (`audiobook-prep`) |\\n    90→| `src/gui/desktop.py` | Tkinter GUI |\\n    91→| `src/gui/tui.py` | Textual-based terminal UI |\\n    92→\\n    93→### Data Models\\n    94→| File | Purpose |\\n    95→|------|---------|\\n    96→| `src/models.py` | Core Pydantic models (AnalysisResult, Character, etc.) |\\n    97→| `src/pipeline/character_extraction/models.py` | Character extraction models |\\n    98→| `src/pipeline/character_profiling/models.py` | Character profiling models |\\n    99→\\n   100→## Configuration\\n   101→\\n   102→### Agent Model Recommendations\\n   103→\\n   104→From `src/agents/config.py`:\\n   105→\\n   106→```python\\n   107→RECOMMENDED_AGENT_MODELS = {\\n   108→    \\\"structure\\\": [\\\"qwen2.5:14b\\\", \\\"qwen2.5:7b\\\", \\\"llama3.2\\\"],\\n   109→    \\\"characters\\\": [\\\"qwen2.5:32b\\\", \\\"qwen2.5:72b\\\", \\\"llama3.1:70b\\\"],\\n   110→    \\\"summaries\\\": [\\\"qwen2.5:32b\\\", \\\"qwen2.5:72b\\\", \\\"llama3.1:70b\\\"],\\n   111→    \\\"pronunciation\\\": [\\\"qwen2.5:14b\\\", \\\"qwen2.5:32b\\\", \\\"llama3.2\\\"],\\n   112→}\\n   113→```\\n   114→\\n   115→### Verification Levels\\n   116→\\n   117→Agents support three verification levels:\\n   118→- `STRUCTURAL` - Fast heuristic checks, no LLM\\n   119→- `SELF_CHECK` - Local LLM validation, book-agnostic\\n   120→- `ORACLE` - Claude-assisted (used by this improvement loop)\\n   121→\\n   122→## Common Issues & Fixes\\n   123→\\n   124→### Ollama Connection\\n   125→```bash\\n   126→# Ensure Ollama is running\\n   127→ollama serve\\n   128→\\n   129→# Check available models\\n   130→ollama list\\n   131→\\n   132→# Pull a model if needed\\n   133→ollama pull qwen2.5:32b\\n   134→```\\n   135→\\n   136→### Out of Memory\\n   137→- Reduce model size: Use 14b instead of 32b\\n   138→- Process shorter texts first\\n   139→- Check GPU memory: `nvidia-smi`\\n   140→\\n   141→### Slow Analysis\\n   142→- Full analysis of a novel can take 10-60 minutes\\n   143→- Use smaller models for faster iteration during development\\n   144→- Check `output/{book}/pipeline.log` for progress\\n   145→\\n   146→## Testing\\n   147→\\n   148→```bash\\n   149→# Run all tests\\n   150→pytest tests/ -v\\n   151→\\n   152→# Run specific agent tests\\n   153→pytest tests/test_character_agent.py -v\\n   154→pytest tests/test_structure_agent.py -v\\n   155→pytest tests/test_summary_agent.py -v\\n   156→pytest tests/test_pronunciation_agent.py -v\\n   157→\\n   158→# Run alias/merging tests\\n   159→pytest tests/test_alias_merging.py -v\\n   160→pytest tests/test_coreference.py -v\\n   161→\\n   162→# Run with coverage\\n   163→pytest tests/ --cov=src --cov-report=html\\n   164→```\\n   165→\\n   166→## Loop-Specific Files\\n   167→\\n   168→| File | Purpose |\\n   169→|------|---------|\\n   170→| `oracle-loop.sh` | Bash orchestrator for the improvement loop |\\n   171→| `PROMPT_analyze.md` | Phase 1 instructions |\\n   172→| `PROMPT_evaluate.md` | Phase 2 oracle evaluation instructions |\\n   173→| `PROMPT_fix.md` | Phase 3 fix instructions |\\n   174→| `manifest.json` | Test text tracking |\\n   175→| `EVALUATION_STATE.md` | Current state and issues |\\n   176→| `spec/output_quality.md` | Quality evaluation rubric |\\n   177→| `logs/` | Iteration logs |\\n   178→\\n\\n<system-reminder>\\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\\n</system-reminder>\\n\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"70ad5c5b-4289-44e9-b3de-238a550757a1\",\"uuid\":\"9b70270c-9e57-4786-986a-3a14e670300e\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"type\":\"text\",\"file\":{\"filePath\":\"/home/zacharymandrews/Tools/audiobook_agent/AGENTS.md\",\"content\":\"# Audiobook Agent - Operational Guide\\n\\nThis guide provides operational commands and codebase navigation for the autonomous improvement loop.\\n\\n## Running the Analysis Pipeline\\n\\n### Basic Commands\\n\\n```bash\\n# Full analysis on a text file with HTML output (use --rich-progress for live updates)\\nvenv/bin/python -m src.cli analyze Test_Texts/gatsby.txt --html output/gatsby/report.html --output output/gatsby/analysis.json --rich-progress\\n\\n# With specific models per agent\\nvenv/bin/python -m src.cli analyze Test_Texts/gatsby.txt \\\\\\n    --structure-model qwen2.5:14b \\\\\\n    --character-model qwen2.5:32b \\\\\\n    --summary-model qwen2.5:32b \\\\\\n    --pronunciation-model qwen2.5:14b \\\\\\n    --html output/gatsby/report.html \\\\\\n    --rich-progress\\n\\n# Set default model for all agents\\nvenv/bin/python -m src.cli analyze Test_Texts/gatsby.txt --llm-model qwen2.5:32b --html output/gatsby/report.html --rich-progress\\n\\n# Adjust minimum character mentions threshold\\nvenv/bin/python -m src.cli analyze Test_Texts/gatsby.txt --min-mentions 3 --html output/gatsby/report.html --rich-progress\\n```\\n\\n### CLI Options\\n\\n| Option | Description | Default |\\n|--------|-------------|---------|\\n| `--output FILE` | JSON output path | `{input_stem}.analysis.json` |\\n| `--html FILE` | HTML report path | None |\\n| `--tui` | Open interactive TUI after analysis | False |\\n| `--wpm N` | Words per minute for duration estimates | 150 |\\n| `--min-mentions N` | Minimum character mentions to include | 2 |\\n| `--llm-model MODEL` | Default model for all agents | System default |\\n| `--structure-model MODEL` | Model for chapter detection | Default |\\n| `--character-model MODEL` | Model for character extraction | Default |\\n| `--summary-model MODEL` | Model for chapter summaries | Default |\\n| `--pronunciation-model MODEL` | Model for pronunciation flags | Default |\\n| `--rich-progress` | Show live-updating progress display | False |\\n\\n## Output Locations\\n\\n```\\noutput/\\n└── {book_name}/\\n    ├── report.html          # HTML report for narrator prep\\n    └── analysis.json        # Full JSON analysis data\\n```\\n\\n## Test Texts\\n\\nAvailable in `Test_Texts/`:\\n- `gatsby.txt` - The Great Gatsby (306 KB)\\n- `Frankenstein_ebook.txt` - Frankenstein (421 KB)\\n- `East of Eden - East Of Eden.pdf` - East of Eden (1.6 MB)\\n- `I_Have_No_Mouth_And_I_Must_Scream.pdf` - Ellison short story (325 KB)\\n- `One Hundred Years of Solitude - One_Hundred_Years_of_Solitude.pdf` - Marquez (1.5 MB)\\n- `See the Light V-15 11-11-25.docx` - Test document (1.2 MB)\\n\\n## Key Source Files\\n\\n### Agent System\\n| File | Purpose |\\n|------|---------|\\n| `src/agents/base.py` | Abstract Agent class with verify/refine methods |\\n| `src/agents/structure.py` | StructureAgent - chapter detection |\\n| `src/agents/characters.py` | CharacterAgent - character extraction & aliases |\\n| `src/agents/summaries.py` | SummaryAgent - chapter summaries |\\n| `src/agents/pronunciation.py` | PronunciationAgent - pronunciation flags |\\n| `src/agents/config.py` | OrchestratorConfig, per-agent model settings |\\n| `src/agents/validation.py` | Upstream validation types |\\n\\n### Pipeline\\n| File | Purpose |\\n|------|---------|\\n| `src/analyzer.py` | Main orchestrator - runs all agents |\\n| `src/pipeline/character_extraction/` | Character NER and extraction |\\n| `src/pipeline/character_profiling/` | Character profile generation |\\n| `src/pipeline/llm.py` | Unified LLM client (Ollama/OpenAI/Anthropic) |\\n| `src/pipeline/metrics.py` | Profiling and metrics |\\n\\n### Entry Points\\n| File | Purpose |\\n|------|---------|\\n| `src/cli.py` | CLI entry point (`audiobook-prep`) |\\n| `src/gui/desktop.py` | Tkinter GUI |\\n| `src/gui/tui.py` | Textual-based terminal UI |\\n\\n### Data Models\\n| File | Purpose |\\n|------|---------|\\n| `src/models.py` | Core Pydantic models (AnalysisResult, Character, etc.) |\\n| `src/pipeline/character_extraction/models.py` | Character extraction models |\\n| `src/pipeline/character_profiling/models.py` | Character profiling models |\\n\\n## Configuration\\n\\n### Agent Model Recommendations\\n\\nFrom `src/agents/config.py`:\\n\\n```python\\nRECOMMENDED_AGENT_MODELS = {\\n    \\\"structure\\\": [\\\"qwen2.5:14b\\\", \\\"qwen2.5:7b\\\", \\\"llama3.2\\\"],\\n    \\\"characters\\\": [\\\"qwen2.5:32b\\\", \\\"qwen2.5:72b\\\", \\\"llama3.1:70b\\\"],\\n    \\\"summaries\\\": [\\\"qwen2.5:32b\\\", \\\"qwen2.5:72b\\\", \\\"llama3.1:70b\\\"],\\n    \\\"pronunciation\\\": [\\\"qwen2.5:14b\\\", \\\"qwen2.5:32b\\\", \\\"llama3.2\\\"],\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Verification Levels\\n\\nAgents support three verification levels:\\n- `STRUCTURAL` - Fast heuristic checks, no LLM\\n- `SELF_CHECK` - Local LLM validation, book-agnostic\\n- `ORACLE` - Claude-assisted (used by this improvement loop)\\n\\n## Common Issues & Fixes\\n\\n### Ollama Connection\\n```bash\\n# Ensure Ollama is running\\nollama serve\\n\\n# Check available models\\nollama list\\n\\n# Pull a model if needed\\nollama pull qwen2.5:32b\\n```\\n\\n### Out of Memory\\n- Reduce model size: Use 14b instead of 32b\\n- Process shorter texts first\\n- Check GPU memory: `nvidia-smi`\\n\\n### Slow Analysis\\n- Full analysis of a novel can take 10-60 minutes\\n- Use smaller models for faster iteration during development\\n- Check `output/{book}/pipeline.log` for progress\\n\\n## Testing\\n\\n```bash\\n# Run all tests\\npytest tests/ -v\\n\\n# Run specific agent tests\\npytest tests/test_character_agent.py -v\\npytest tests/test_structure_agent.py -v\\npytest tests/test_summary_agent.py -v\\npytest tests/test_pronunciation_agent.py -v\\n\\n# Run alias/merging tests\\npytest tests/test_alias_merging.py -v\\npytest tests/test_coreference.py -v\\n\\n# Run with coverage\\npytest tests/ --cov=src --cov-report=html\\n```\\n\\n## Loop-Specific Files\\n\\n| File | Purpose |\\n|------|---------|\\n| `oracle-loop.sh` | Bash orchestrator for the improvement loop |\\n| `PROMPT_analyze.md` | Phase 1 instructions |\\n| `PROMPT_evaluate.md` | Phase 2 oracle evaluation instructions |\\n| `PROMPT_fix.md` | Phase 3 fix instructions |\\n| `manifest.json` | Test text tracking |\\n| `EVALUATION_STATE.md` | Current state and issues |\\n| `spec/output_quality.md` | Quality evaluation rubric |\\n| `logs/` | Iteration logs |\\n\",\"numLines\":178,\"startLine\":1,\"totalLines\":178}}}\n--\n{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929\",\"id\":\"msg_014G2bczdcnJxqiZAE9DAJ6W\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01B5uZq8pZ16rGovQhWteJrm\",\"name\":\"TodoWrite\",\"input\":{\"todos\":[{\"content\":\"Read evaluation state and understand critical issue\",\"activeForm\":\"Reading evaluation state and understanding critical issue\",\"status\":\"completed\"},{\"content\":\"Perform root cause analysis - trace data flow for mummer/Prospero merge\",\"activeForm\":\"Performing root cause analysis - tracing data flow\",\"status\":\"in_progress\"},{\"content\":\"Add diagnostic logging to verify execution path\",\"activeForm\":\"Adding diagnostic logging to verify execution path\",\"status\":\"pending\"},{\"content\":\"Run smoke test on first 2-3 chapters\",\"activeForm\":\"Running smoke test on first 2-3 chapters\",\"status\":\"pending\"},{\"content\":\"Implement targeted fix based on root cause\",\"activeForm\":\"Implementing targeted fix based on root cause\",\"status\":\"pending\"},{\"content\":\"Update EVALUATION_STATE.md with findings\",\"activeForm\":\"Updating EVALUATION_STATE.md with findings\",\"status\":\"pending\"},{\"content\":\"Commit changes with detailed explanation\",\"activeForm\":\"Committing changes with detailed explanation\",\"status\":\"pending\"}]}}],\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":6,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":13203,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":23343,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":13203,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":1,\"service_tier\":\"standard\"},\"context_management\":n