n   - Evidence: Chapter summary CORRECTLY identifies two characters: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Prince Prospero\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" and \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"The masked figure (Red Death)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" - but character extraction merges them\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   - Impact: Major character missing from analysis\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   - Note: Will emerge naturally once issue #1 is fixed\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n### HIGH\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n3. **Missing alias: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"the duke\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" for Prince Prospero**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   - Problem: Text uses \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"the duke\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" to refer to Prospero: \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"as might have been expected from the duke's love of the bizarre\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   - Location: Alias detection\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n4. **Mention count too low for Prince Prospero**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   - Problem: Character shows 6 mentions, but pronunciation shows 18 \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Prospero\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" + 9 \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Prince\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" occurrences\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   - Evidence: Clear discrepancy between pronunciation counting and character counting\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   - Location: Mention count aggregation in character pipeline\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n### MEDIUM\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n5. **Canonical name format includes leading article**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   - Problem: Character name is \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"the Prince Prospero\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" instead of \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Prince Prospero\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   - Location: Character name normalization\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n6. **Too many common words in pronunciation guide (65+ in \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"Other\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\")**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   - P