\\\\\\\\\\\\n- Death relationship detection (attempt 8)\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**None have worked.** The merge is happening despite ALL of these fixes.\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n### Hypotheses for Why Fixes Keep Failing\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n1. **The merge may happen BEFORE cross-group resolution**: The epithet \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"the mummer\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" may be classified and merged at an earlier pipeline stage before any of our checks run\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n2. **The LLM merge decision is overriding all rules**: Even with explicit blocking code, the final merge decision may be bypassing these checks\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n3. **Logging gap**: We haven't verified that the blocking code is actually being called. Need to add explicit debug logging to trace the exact point where the merge decision is made\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n4. **The fix code may not be in the execution path**: The `_entities_in_death_relationship()` and `_entities_in_confrontation()` functions may exist but never be invoked\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n### Recommended Next Approach\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n**STOP adding new detection code until we verify existing code is being called.**\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n1. **Add trace logging at EVERY decision point** in the character extraction pipeline:\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   - Log when epithet candidates are generated\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   - Log when cross-group resolution is called\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   - Log when confrontation/death checks are executed\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   - Log the exact LLM prompt and response for the merge decision\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n   - Log the final merge output\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n2. **Identify the EXACT line of code** where \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"the mummer\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" gets added to Prince Prospero's alias list\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\n3. **Consider fundamentally different approach**: