{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929","id":"msg_01X7HtYdqh8mX2zJRxr4fu83","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014x4JJi5u4WJk8tUQYQxnim","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/home/zacharymandrews/Tools/audiobook_agent/EVALUATION_STATE.md","old_string":"## Attempt 8 Fix Assessment\n\n### Fix: Hard-coded death relationship detection\n**Status: DID NOT WORK**\n\nThe fix from attempt 8 added `_entities_in_death_relationship()` function to detect when one entity dies at the hands of another. This was meant to block the merge of \"the mummer\" with \"Prince Prospero\" based on the text:\n- \"fell prostrate in death the Prince Prospero\" (Prospero dies)\n- \"seizing the mummer\" (after Prospero confronts the mummer)\n\n**Result:** \"the mummer\" is STILL incorrectly merged with \"Prince Prospero\"\n\n**Evidence from analysis.json:**\n- Character: \"the Prince Prospero\"\n- Aliases: [\"the mummer\"]\n- Only 1 character detected (should be 2)\n\n**Why it failed:** Possible reasons:\n1. The death relationship function may not be getting called\n2. The merge may be happening at an earlier pipeline stage\n3. The function's pattern matching may not be capturing the actual text patterns\n4. The merge decision may be bypassing the death relationship check","new_string":"## Attempt 9 Fix Assessment\n\n### Root Cause Analysis (CONFIRMED):\nAfter tracing the complete data flow, the issue is:\n\n1. **\"the mummer\"** has only 3 mentions in the text\n2. The critical 3rd mention is: \"seizing the mummer, whose tall figure stood erect...\"\n3. This mention occurs ~150 characters AFTER \"fell prostrate in death the Prince Prospero\"\n4. **The context window was only 100 chars per mention**, so the death scene was SPLIT across windows\n5. The LLM never saw both entities AND the death in the same context\n6. The post-hoc death checks (attempts 4, 8) failed for the same reason - 100-char windows\n\n**Why previous attempts failed:**\n- Attempt 3-5, 7: LLM prompt rules couldn't work because LLM didn't see the full scene\n- Attempt 4, 8: Post-hoc code checks couldn't work because they used the same 100-char windows\n- Attempt 7: Increased context to 400 chars TOTAL (4 contexts × 100 each) - still too small\n\n### Fix Applied:\n1. **Increased context window for cross-group resolution:**\n   - Epithets: 400 → **800 chars** (4 contexts × 200 each)\n   - Proper names: 400 → **600 chars** (3 contexts × 200 each)\n   - This ensures death/confrontation scenes spanning 150+ chars are captured\n\n2. **Added explicit death rule to LLM prompt (CRITICAL RULE #6):**\n   - \"DO NOT link if one entity DIES in interaction with the other entity\"\n   - Provides examples: \"fell prostrate in death\", \"killed by\"\n   - Makes the death prohibition explicit alongside the confrontation rule\n\n**Files modified:**\n- `src/pipeline/character_extraction/consensus.py:96-117` (added rule #6 to CROSS_GROUP_SYSTEM)\n- `src/pipeline/character_extraction/consensus.py:2205` (increased epithet context to 800)\n- `src/pipeline/character_extraction/consensus.py:2220` (increased proper name context to 600)\n\n**Expected outcome:**\nThe LLM will now see the full death scene: \"fell prostrate in death the Prince Prospero. Then... seizing the mummer\" in a single 200-char context window, and will apply rule #6 to prevent the merge."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":282,"cache_read_input_tokens":96504,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":282,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":25,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"70ad5c5b-4289-44e9-b3de-238a550757a1","uuid":"b8b64afb-fff0-4558-838e-9d333519d4f4"}
